  "narrative": {
    "intro": "V2X Aerospace has $1.4B in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. V2X Aerospace won 97 awards so far this fiscal year, with an average award size of $14M. Obligations fell 11.7% year over year. Annual obligations rose from $958M in FY21 to $1.1B in FY22, then moved through $1B in FY23 and $1.2B in FY24 before reaching $1.5B in FY25 and $1.4B in FY26. The Department of Defense is the largest buyer at $1B, followed by the General Services Administration at $287M and the Department of Justice at $32.6M. Other notable buying agencies in FY2026 to date include the Department of Homeland Security at $10.4M and the National Aeronautics and Space Administration at $2.7M. The biggest NAICS markets are Other Support Activities for Air Transportation at $945M and Engineering Services at $333M. V2X Aerospace also sells in Aircraft Manufacturing at $39.2M, All Other Professional, Scientific, and Technical Services at $20.8M, and Other Scientific and Technical Consulting Services at $20.1M. FY2026 totals are partial fiscal-year figures.",
    "sections": [
